<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch01-velocity-distance-and-the-first-shape-of-calculus">
  <title>Velocity, Distance, and the First Shape of Calculus</title>
  <shorttitle>Velocity and Distance</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>Velocity describes how position changes with time. Accumulating velocity over a time interval gives the change in position. This chapter develops these two relationships using motion, slopes, areas, finite differences, and finite sums.</p></introduction>

